% Section 5 — Runtime Analysis
% Data source: artifacts/rebuttal/w3_runtime_report.md
% Per-document inference times from JSONL outputs (inference_time_seconds field).
% All runs on same single-GPU server (westd-16980), same vLLM/transformers stack.

\subsection{Runtime Overhead}
\label{sec:runtime}

Table~\ref{tab:runtime} reports per-document inference time for each configuration.

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\small
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{4pt}
\begin{tabular}{@{}lll rr@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Model} & \textbf{Dataset} & \textbf{Mode} & \textbf{Avg (s)} & \textbf{Overhead} \\
\midrule
\multirow{3}{*}{Qwen}
  & \multirow{3}{*}{SciERC}
    & Unconstrained & 8.69 & --- \\
  & & Grammar       & 8.82 & $+$1.4\% \\
  & & Full (S1)     & 6.76 & $-$22.2\% \\
\cmidrule(l){2-5}
\multirow{2}{*}{}
  & \multirow{2}{*}{DocRED}
    & Unconstrained & 19.76 & --- \\
  & & Full (S1)     & 20.40 & $+$3.2\% \\
\midrule
\multirow{2}{*}{Llama}
  & SciERC
    & Unconstrained & 2.81 & --- \\
  & & Full (S1)     & 4.33 & $+$53.8\% \\
\cmidrule(l){2-5}
  & \multirow{2}{*}{DocRED}
    & Unconstrained & 18.16 & --- \\
  & & Full (S1)     & 20.52 & $+$13.0\% \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\caption{Per-document inference time (wall-clock seconds, same GPU).
Grammar-only overhead is $\leq$4.2\% (Qwen; Llama grammar-only not separately measured).
Post-hoc filtering is an $O(n)$ pass over predicted triples and adds negligible time.}
\label{tab:runtime}
\end{table}

Overhead ranges from $-$22\% to $+$54\%, with three of four cells at $\leq$13\%; the outlier (Llama-SciERC, $+$53.8\%) is only $+$1.5\,s absolute.
Qwen-SciERC exhibits a \emph{speedup} ($-$22.2\%) because constrained decoding produces tighter outputs, avoiding long noisy continuations before EOS.
Grammar-only overhead is $\leq$4.2\% (Qwen), indicating the semantic layer's logit masking accounts for most incremental cost.
Llama grammar-only was not separately measured; because the grammar layer uses identical DFA construction across models, Qwen's $\leq$4.2\% provides a reasonable proxy.

